{# ── Chapter: Takeaway ── #}
<section class="case-chapter" data-chapter="takeaway">
  <h2>Remember</h2>
  <div class="case-takeaway">
    <h3>Key takeaways</h3>
    <ul>
      <li>
        <div class="tone-junior">A JS variable isn't a cache — it's gone the instant the page reloads. IndexedDB actually persists structured data across reloads and works without a network.</div>
        <div class="tone-mid">Write every successful fetch into an IndexedDB read model, then read from IndexedDB first on load and revalidate over the network in the background — stale data beats a blank screen.</div>
        <div class="tone-staff">Keep async work outside the transaction boundary — a transaction auto-commits once it has no pending requests, and awaiting unrelated work inside it throws TransactionInactiveError. Reach for it only where losing data on reload genuinely costs something; cheap-to-refetch data doesn't need it.</div>
      </li>
    </ul>
  </div>
</section>
